phonebook 0.1

# Every float reads back from its shortest text and prints the same way in
# every backend. Each backend takes its digits from its own host (Python's repr,
# Rust's {:e}) and lays them out by hand, so this sweep is what would notice
# if the two hosts ever picked different shortest digits. The values are fixed;
# they were drawn once from random bit patterns plus a list of known hard cases.
#
# The first line is the case that caught a real divergence: each of these sits
# exactly halfway between two shortest candidates. Rust's {:e} picks the upper
# one; the contract, like Python's repr, picks the one ending in an even digit.

ext 000-0000001 ROUND_TRIP (cell: text) -> text {
  400-0000022@[cell, 0.0] -> value      # PARSE_FLOAT
  100-0000005@[value] -> rendered       # TO_TEXT
  return rendered
}

